                "quoted_status_profile_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 47,
                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "I know how important healthcare is to American families. That\u2019s why I\u2019m working with my colleagues to protect and strengthen Medicare and Medicaid. Let\u2019s talk about one of the biggest Medicaid reforms that Democrats have highlighted in the tax reconciliation bill. Our bill creates a new work requirement for healthy working-age adults without children. This work (or community) engagement requirement will require healthy working-age adults without children to either work, volunteer, or attend college/vocational training for at least 20 hours a week. I believe this is a reasonable reform to Medicaid because it strengthens the program for the disabled, children, parents, and seniors the program was designed to help. It also protects taxpayers. I don\u2019t believe it\u2019s fair to ask a taxpayer who works 40 hours a week to support their family to have their tax dollars go towards providing Medicaid benefits for healthy working-age adults without children who refuse to work. I simply disagree with Democrats who want taxpayers to keep paying for the status quo and oppose this reasonable work requirement.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1751415522,
                "view_count": 1758
